# 64Forth — LLDB: do not stop on memory faults from the Forth kernel.
# The kernel installs SIGSEGV/SIGBUS handlers that siglongjmp back to the REPL
# (same idea as TZForth soft throws). Without this, Xcode stops in the debugger
# on EXC_BAD_ACCESS before the Unix signal is delivered to the process.
#
# Wired via the 64Forth shared scheme: customLLDBInitFile.
process handle SIGSEGV -n true -p true -s false
process handle SIGBUS  -n true -p true -s false
